From d35a04494e6fc25ea8d6a045e7e5d6d4884bfe9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: sm5703-charger: notify on every cable change

sm5703_charger_extcon_work() only calls power_supply_changed() when
sm5703_charger_apply_input_current() reports that it actually wrote a new
limit.

Unplugging an SDP port hits the case where it does not: the limit for "no
cable" and the limit for an SDP port are both the conservative 500 mA, so
the register already holds the right value and nothing is announced -
even though ONLINE has just gone from 1 to 0.  No uevent reaches
userspace, UPower only notices at its next poll, and the charging icon
takes some fifteen seconds to disappear.

What changed is the cable, not just the limit, so announce it either way.
The register write is still skipped when there is nothing to write.
---
 drivers/power/supply/sm5703-charger.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/sm5703-charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/sm5703-charger.c
index cc017b75b4..19725e2a3e 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sm5703-charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sm5703-charger.c
@@ -510,8 +510,7 @@ static void sm5703_charger_extcon_work(struct work_struct *work)
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if (ret)
-		power_supply_changed(chg->psy);
+	power_supply_changed(chg->psy);
 }
 
 static int sm5703_charger_extcon_notify(struct notifier_block *nb,
-- 
